<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
    <AssemblyName>Clast.Fsst</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>Clast.Fsst</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Label="Package metadata">
    <PackageId>Clast.Fsst</PackageId>
    <!-- Local default only; release.yml packs with -p:Version=<tag>. -->
    <Version>0.3.1</Version>
    <!-- Held across the whole 0.3.x line so consumers don't need a binding
         redirect per patch. Under 0.x semver the minor is the breaking slot,
         so bump this to 0.4.0.0 at the next breaking release. Hardcoded rather
         than derived from $(Version), which the release tag overrides. -->
    <AssemblyVersion>0.3.0.0</AssemblyVersion>
    <!-- FileVersion would otherwise default to the pinned AssemblyVersion; track
         the real version so builds stay distinguishable. Skipped for prerelease
         values, which are not valid Win32 file versions. -->
    <FileVersion Condition="!$(Version.Contains('-'))">$(Version)</FileVersion>
    <Authors>clast-project</Authors>
    <Company>clast-project</Company>
    <Description>FSST (Fast Static Symbol Table) string compression for .NET. Supports the FSST8 (1-byte codes), FSST12 (12-bit codes) and FSST16 (2-byte codes) variants.</Description>
    <PackageTags>fsst;compression;string;columnar;dictionary</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>0.3.1 fixes FSST8 data corruption on write. Upgrade from 0.3.0 is strongly recommended.

- SymbolTable.Finalize could assign one code to two symbols, whenever a trained table held both a length-2 symbol that is a prefix of a longer symbol and a length-3 symbol. One symbol was lost, and the compressor emitted its code for input matching the other — so compressing and decompressing with the same table returned altered bytes. Present since 0.1.0, but only reachable from tables 0.3.0's ratio fixes started producing.
- FSST8 data written by 0.3.0 cannot be recovered and must be re-encoded from source; the lost symbol is absent from the exported table. An affected table also exports a length histogram inconsistent with its symbol payload, so ImportFsst8 on it throws rather than loading. Reading data written by 0.2.0 and earlier was never affected, nor was FSST12 or FSST16, which have no code-renumbering pass.
- Recovering the lost symbols also recovers the compression they were costing: 3.50x to 4.58x on a synthetic URL corpus.

0.3.0 adds FSST16 (2-byte codes, up to 65,535 symbols, symbols up to 16 bytes) — the variant the Parquet FSST proposal calls FSST_16.

Breaking:
- TryDecompress now returns false for malformed input as well as a too-small destination, where it previously decoded as much as it could. The new Decompress overload returns OperationStatus so the two are distinguishable, and the allocating overloads throw InvalidDataException on corruption.
- FSST8 and FSST12 produce different compressed bytes, as a result of the ratio fixes below. Data written by earlier versions still decodes; no reader change is needed.

Fixes, all affecting compression ratio:
- FSST8 length-2 symbols were in the table but unreachable when compressing.
- Probe symbols carried a zeroed code field, making any symbol whose length matched the available input unreachable unless its code was 0 — every length-8 symbol, and every symbol at the end of a short value. Affected FSST8 and FSST12.
- The pair-frequency counter overflowed past 3,840 occurrences into an adjacent pair's slot, inventing symbols absent from the input.

Measured on a synthetic URL corpus: FSST8 1.93x to 3.11x, FSST12 2.07x to 2.71x. Compression is 2.7-3.0x faster and FSST12 training 3.1x.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>Apache-2.0</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/clast-project/fsst</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/clast-project/fsst</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Label="SourceLink + symbols">
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <DebugType>portable</DebugType>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub" Version="8.0.0" PrivateAssets="all" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'netstandard2.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="System.Memory" Version="4.5.5" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Fsst.Tests" Key="$(ClastPublicKey)" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
